'''Chilled jellies''' are stronger variants of [[Jelly|jellies]] that require level 52 [[Slayer]] to kill. They also require either completion of [[The Heart of Darkness]] or level 87 [[Sailing]] to reach, due to their locations: within the [[Ruins of Tapoyauik]] and inside the [[Grimstone dungeon|dungeon]] on [[Grimstone]]. 

In most respects, they are identical to [[Warped Jelly|warped jellies]]. However, they have a 50% [[Elemental weakness|fire weakness]] and do not drop [[Ancient shard|ancient shards]] and [[Dark totem piece|dark totem pieces]] (although if they are killed in the [[Ruins of Tapoyauik]] they will drop [[Frozen tear|frozen tears]] and [[Tooth half of key (moon key)|tooth halves of moon keys]] instead). Like all [[Jelly|jellies]], Chilled jellies have a chance to spawn their respective [[Vitreous Jelly]] on death, in this case a [[Vitreous Chilled Jelly]], if the ''Bigger and Badder'' [[Slayer Rewards|Slayer unlock]] is enabled.

Jellies attack with [[magical melee]], so armour with high magic defence is recommended, such as [[Karil's armour]] or [[black dragonhide armour]]. Like their lower levelled counterparts, using [[Protect from Melee]] will prevent all damage from them. 

They can be safespotted in the Ruins of Tapoyauik between the two icicles to the north or to the east using Ranged or Magic.

